HST Office: in the Styles gallery, the keyboard cursor follows the selected preview.

Every page of the gallery is refilled from scratch, which leaves the icon view without a keyboard
cursor; selecting the current style's preview does not set one. An arrow key inside the page then
started from the page's first preview (Right) or last (Left) instead of the selected one. With two
previews per page, Left after paging back stayed on the same style, and Right after paging on did too.
UpdateSelection now puts the cursor on the preview it selects (set_cursor sends no selection signal).

- svx StylesPreviewWindow: UpdateSelection sets the cursor.

License: these upstream files remain under their original license (MPL-2.0).
---
--- a/svx/source/tbxctrls/StylesPreviewWindow.cxx
+++ b/svx/source/tbxctrls/StylesPreviewWindow.cxx
@@ -1072,13 +1072,19 @@
     const size_t nEnd = std::min(m_aAllStyles.size(), m_nFirstVisible + m_nPageSize);
     for (StylePreviewList::size_type i = m_nFirstVisible; i < nEnd; ++i)
     {
         if (m_aAllStyles[i].commonName == m_sSelectedStyle
             || m_aAllStyles[i].translatedName == m_sSelectedStyle)
         {
-            m_xStylesView->select(i - m_nFirstVisible);
+            const int nPos = static_cast<int>(i - m_nFirstVisible);
+            m_xStylesView->select(nPos);
+            // HST Office: the keyboard cursor follows the selection. A page is refilled from scratch,
+            // which leaves the view without a cursor, and an arrow key then starts from the page's
+            // first (Right) or last (Left) preview instead of the selected one, so it did nothing.
+            if (std::unique_ptr<weld::TreeIter> xIter = m_xStylesView->get_iterator(nPos))
+                m_xStylesView->set_cursor(*xIter);
             return;
         }
     }
     m_xStylesView->unselect_all();
 }
 
